          "id": "note",
          "kind": "note",
          "data": {
            "text": "## Trunked talkgroups\n\n**DMR trunk system** is not a decoder you tune. Give it the control channel and it follows the traffic itself: it reads which talkgroup moved to which frequency and decodes the voice there. One node instead of a channel per slot.\n\nDiscovery is on, so it probes for the control channel rather than waiting to be told.\n\n**Audio FX** cleans what comes out. Trunked voice is often clipped and noisy; the filter and denoise settings here are worth more than on broadcast audio.\n\n**Audio recorder** keeps the calls, skipping the silence between them.\n\n**Decoder log** records who called which talkgroup and when, which is the part you search later.\n\nSet the Device to your local DMR control channel."
          },
          "position": { "x": 0.0, "y": 420.0 }
        }
